  triage:title "boundary_enforcement.rs writer-surface scan omits the legacy v1 bridge" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs:472-505 (task_mutation_cannot_restore_a_second_message_write_pipeline) scans only task_mutation_store.rs and writer/task_ops.rs as 'writer_surfaces,' omitting writer/task_legacy_ops.rs -- itself a SQLite task writer module per its own doc comment and explicitly named in AZ.2's affected paths. D5 requires this mechanical scan to cover the SQLite task writer surfaces (plural); the legacy v1 bridge write path is left unguarded by this specific tripwire. Related to AZS2-RBQA-002 (same governance-gap pattern). Confirmed at head 6937c547f. Fix: add writer/task_legacy_ops.rs to the writer_surfaces list scanned by task_mutation_cannot_restore_a_second_message_write_pipeline. Source: QA-1 on PR #1382 (https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1382#issuecomment-5612459494)." ;
